{
  "has_animal_human_comparison": false,
  "evidence": "The study reports on IRAK3 mRNA expression in human in vivo studies, increases of IRAK3 mRNA expression in rodent models, increases of TNF-α and IL-6 protein levels in human in vivo models, elevation of TNF-α and IL-6 in rodents, the effect of IRAK3 in inhibiting TNF-α mRNA expression in mice, and the effect of IRAK3 on protein expression of TNF-α and IL-6 in mice. It also reports on increases of IRAK3 mRNA and protein expression in rodent in vivo studies, and decreases of TNF-α and IL-6 protein levels in humans following two challenges compared to one. Finally, it reports on decreases of TNF-α protein levels in mice after two challenges compared to one, and the inhibitory effect of IRAK3 on TNF-α mRNA and protein levels in mice after two challenges.",
  "comparison_type": "none-found",
  "reason": "The study includes separate analyses of animal (rodent, mouse) and human data, but no direct quantitative comparison between animal and human results is reported. For example, there is no comparison of the sensitivity or specificity of an animal model for predicting a human outcome, nor a comparison of treatment effects between animal models and human clinical trials."
